76800>>>>>Define FILE_ATTRIBUTE_TEMPORARY             for 256 // a file that is being used for temporary storage. File systems avoid writing data back to mass storage If sufficient cache memory is available, because typically, an application deletes a temporary file after the Handle is closed. In that scenario, the system can entirely avoid writing the data. Otherwise, the data is written after the Handle is closed.
