80507>>>>>Class cDRReportHelper is a cObject
80508>>>>>    // The AddFilter function expects a string. If you move a DateTime to a string the format
80508>>>>>    // is incorrect for SQL. With this function we can convert the DateTime to string in the appropriate
80508>>>>>    // format (this is yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm:ss)). The prefix zeroes are important.
80508>>>>>    Function DateTimeToString DateTime dtIn Returns String
80510>>>>>        String sDateTimeResult
80510>>>>>
80510>>>>>        Move (DateGetYear (dtIn)) to sDateTimeResult
80511>>>>>        Move (sDateTimeResult - '-' - (Right ('0' + String (DateGetMonth (dtIn)), 2))) to sDateTimeResult
80512>>>>>        Move (sDateTimeResult - '-' - (Right ('0' + String (DateGetDay (dtIn)), 2))) to sDateTimeResult
80513>>>>>        Move (sDateTimeResult * (Right ('0' + String (DateGetHour (dtIn)), 2))) to sDateTimeResult
80514>>>>>        Move (sDateTimeResult - ':' - (Right ('0' + String (DateGetMinute (dtIn)), 2))) to sDateTimeResult
80515>>>>>        Move (sDateTimeResult - ':' - (Right ('0' + String (DateGetSecond (dtIn)), 2))) to sDateTimeResult
80516>>>>>
80516>>>>>        Function_Return sDateTimeResult
80517>>>>>    End_Function
80518>>>>>
80518>>>>>    // The AddFilter function expects a string. If you move a Date to a string the format
80518>>>>>    // is incorrect for SQL. With this function we can convert the Date to string first in the appropriate
80518>>>>>    // format (this is yyyy-mm-dd). The prefix zero's are important.
80518>>>>>    Function DateToString Date dIn Returns String
80520>>>>>        String sDateResult
80520>>>>>        DateTime dtIn
80520>>>>>
80520>>>>>        Move dIn to dtIn
80521>>>>>        Move (DateGetYear (dtIn)) to sDateResult
80522>>>>>        Move (sDateResult - '-' - (Right ('0' + String (DateGetMonth (dtIn)), 2))) to sDateResult
80523>>>>>        Move (sDateResult - '-' - (Right ('0' + String (DateGetDay (dtIn)), 2))) to sDateResult
80524>>>>>
80524>>>>>        Function_Return sDateResult
80525>>>>>    End_Function
80526>>>>>
80526>>>>>    // Use this function to convert a time variable to string. Should be used for psParameterValue.
80526>>>>>    Function TimeToString Time tmIn Returns String
80528>>>>>        String sTimeResult
80528>>>>>        DateTime dtIn
80528>>>>>
80528>>>>>        Move tmIn to dtIn
80529>>>>>        Move (Right ('0' + String (DateGetHour (dtIN)), 2)) to sTimeResult
80530>>>>>        Move (sTimeResult + ':' + Right ('0' + String (DateGetMinute (dtIn)), 2)) to sTimeResult
80531>>>>>        Move (sTimeResult + ':' + Right ('0' + String (DateGetSecond (dtIn)), 2)) to sTimeResult
80532>>>>>
80532>>>>>        Function_Return sTimeResult
80533>>>>>    End_Function
80534>>>>>End_Class
