87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>//*** Command: SQLConnect                                                   ***
87000>>>>>//*** Purpose: Connect to a server for embedded SQL usage.                  ***
87000>>>>>//***                                                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*** Syntax : SQLConnect To hdbc                                           ***
87000>>>>>//***          SQLConnect [sDriverId sConnectString] To hdbc                ***
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>//*** Command: SQLFileConnect                                               ***
87000>>>>>//*** Purpsoe: Return the handle to a connection of an open file. This      ***
87000>>>>>//***          connection is (obviously) already opened. We are just using  ***
87000>>>>>//***          the same connection for Embedded SQL. This allows the        ***
87000>>>>>//***          programmer not to know connection details.                   ***
87000>>>>>//***                                                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*** Syntax : SQLFileConnect Filex To hdbc                                 ***
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>//*** Command: SQLDisconnect                                                ***
87000>>>>>//*** Purpose: Connect to a server for embedded SQL usage.                  ***
87000>>>>>//***                                                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*** Syntax : SQLDisConnect hdbc                                           ***
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>//*** Command: SQLOpen                                                      ***
87000>>>>>//*** Purpose: Allocate the memory to stroe statement information.          ***
87000>>>>>//***                                                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*** Syntax : SQLOpen hdbc To hstmt                                        ***
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>//*** Command: SQLClose                                                     ***
87000>>>>>//*** Purpose: Close a statement and free all associated memory.            ***
87000>>>>>//***                                                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*** Syntax : SQLClose hstmt                                               ***
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>//*** Command: SQLPrepare                                                   ***
87000>>>>>//*** Purpose: Prepare a statement for execution.                           ***
87000>>>>>//***                                                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*** Syntax : SQLPrepare hstmt sStatement                                  ***
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>//*** Command: SQLExecute                                                   ***
87000>>>>>//*** Purpose: Execute a prepared statement                                 ***
87000>>>>>//***                                                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*** Syntax : SQLExecute hstmt                                             ***
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>//*** Command: SQLExecDirect                                                ***
87000>>>>>//*** Purpose: Prepare and execute a statement.                             ***
87000>>>>>//***                                                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*** Syntax : SQLExecDirect hstmt sStatement                               ***
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>//*** Command: SQLFileFetch                                                 ***
87000>>>>>//*** Purpose: Get a row from a statement result set.                       ***
87000>>>>>//***                                                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*** Syntax : SQLFileFetch hstmt [To File1 [File2 ...]]                    ***
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>//*** Command: SQLBindFetchFile                                             ***
87000>>>>>//*** Purpose: Binds a file number to a statement so it can be used for     ***
87000>>>>>//***          fetching data. Only needed in non fileconnect. Note that     ***
87000>>>>>//***          can be assigned to the connection or the statement handle    ***
87000>>>>>//***                                                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*** Syntax : SQLBindFileForFetch hstmt|hdbc FileName|FileNumber           ***
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>//*** Command: SQLFetch                                                     ***
87000>>>>>//*** Purpose: Get a row from a statement result set.                       ***
87000>>>>>//***                                                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*** Syntax : SQLFetch hstmt [To Var1 [Var2 ...]]                          ***
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>//*** Command: SQLGetData                                                   ***
87000>>>>>//*** Purpose: Get a column's data.                                         ***
87000>>>>>//***                                                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*** Syntax : SQLGetData hstmt iColumnNUmber [Length iLen] To Var          ***
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>//*** Command: SQLColumnMap                                                 ***
87000>>>>>//*** Purpose: Determine the column number based on the column name.        ***
87000>>>>>//***                                                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*** Syntax : SQLColumnMap hstmt sColName To iColNumber                    ***
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>//*** Command: SQLColAttribute                                              ***
87000>>>>>//*** Purpose: Get an attribute of a column in a statements result set.     ***
87000>>>>>//***                                                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*** Syntax : SQLColAttribute hstmt iCol iAttrId To sAttrib                ***
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>//*** Command: SQLStmtAttribute                                             ***
87000>>>>>//*** Purpose: Get an atribute of a statement.                              ***
87000>>>>>//***                                                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*** Syntax : SQLStmtAttribute hstmt iAttribId To sAttrib                  ***
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>//*** Command: SQLCall                                                      ***
87000>>>>>//*** Purpose: Call a stored procedure.                                     ***
87000>>>>>//***                                                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*** Syntax : SQLCall hstmt ProcedureName [Arg1 ...] [To Var]              ***
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>//*** Command: SQLGetArguments                                              ***
87000>>>>>//*** Purpsoe: Get the arguments of a stored procedure. This command should ***
87000>>>>>//***          be used when a procedure has multiple result sets. Some      ***
87000>>>>>//***          backends (SQL SErver for example) will return these as the   ***
87000>>>>>//***          last result set. This emans you first process all other      ***
87000>>>>>//***          result sets and then get the arguments and return value.     ***
87000>>>>>//***                                                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*** Syntax : SQLGetArguments hstmt [Arg1...] [To Var]                     ***
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>//*** Command: SQLNextResultSet                                             ***
87000>>>>>//*** Purpose: Go the the next result set. This command should be used when ***
87000>>>>>//***          a procedure call results in multiple result sets. Processing ***
87000>>>>>//***          such procedures can be done by loping through the result     ***
87000>>>>>//***          sets.                                                        ***
87000>>>>>//***                                                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*** Syntax : SQLNextResultSet hstmt                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
87000>>>>>//*** Command: SQLFetchActivatesBuffer                                      ***
87000>>>>>//*** Purpose: Setup fetch behavior for a file. When set to true a          ***
87000>>>>>//***          succesfull fetch of the statement resutl set will            ***
87000>>>>>//***          automatically set the status of the file's bufer to          ***
87000>>>>>//***          DF_FILE_ACTIVE.                                              ***
87000>>>>>//***                                                                       ***
87000>>>>>//*** Syntax : SQLFetchActivatesBuffer hstmt FileNUmber|FileName sState     ***
87000>>>>>//*****************************************************************************
